      <div class="practitioner-name">Jenny</div>
      <div class="practitioner-role">Yoga & Sound Healing</div>
      <p class="practitioner-bio">Jenny is a Registered Yoga Teacher (RYT) with Yoga Alliance, bringing over a decade of dedicated experience in yoga practice and teaching, with particular expertise in Therapeutic Yoga and Restorative Yoga. She has guided a diverse range of students and has been actively involved in leading and contributing to numerous 200-hour and 500-hour Yoga Teacher Training programmes, with Restorative Yoga as a core component of her curriculum. In recent years she has expanded her practice into Sound Healing, completing extensive training in therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation. Known for her calm presence and authentic approach, these skills inform every class she teaches and every joint session she delivers with Seb. Beyond her practice and teaching, Jenny is an initiate of the Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Matsyendranatha, Gorakhnath, Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="practitioner-card">
      <img src="/img/Ssq.jpg" alt="Seb" class="practitioner-photo">
      <div class="practitioner-name">Seb</div>
      <div class="practitioner-role">Qigong & Raja Yoga</div>
      <p class="practitioner-bio">Seb brings over two decades of training in Asian healing arts. He has practised Yoga since 1997, studying with masters in Japan and India, and is a certified Yoga teacher through IYF Asia, qualified in South Korea. Since 2010 he has trained extensively in authentic Qigong, studying and practising with masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland. He is also a certified Therapeutic Thai bodywork therapist and instructor, accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018, and holds a certificate in Advanced TCM Reflexology. His deep understanding of Qi cultivation, the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine as they relate to energy work, and hands-on therapeutic bodywork informs every class he teaches and every joint session he delivers with Jenny. Beyond the realm of practice and teaching, Seb is an initiate, direct disciple and custodian of the Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Matsyendranatha, Gorakhnath, Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>
    </div>
